.TH smi-neo4j-create-db "1" "November 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-neo4j-create-db \- Create an empty embedded Neo4j Community Edition database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-neo4j-create-db
.RB [ \-d
.IR DIR ]
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-neo4j-create-db
creates the embedded Neo4j database directory
.IB DIR / NAME
and prints, on standard output, the variables to use it, as
.B export
lines for
.B eval
or a file to source:
.BR SMI_DB_TYPE ,
.B SMI_DB_NAME
and
.BR SMI_NEO4J_HOME ,
the absolute path that
.BR smi-neo4j-query (1)
reads.
.PP
The database is embedded: no server runs, the process that opens the directory is the database,
and only one process can open it at a time. Community Edition has the one database
.B neo4j
and no users, so there is nothing to log in with; the rights are those of the directory.
.PP
Creating and querying are separate commands, so the database is created once and queried, or
populated, as many times as needed.
.PP
The command is a Groovy script,
.I neo4j.groovy
in the SMI lib directory, that takes Neo4j and picocli with
.BR @Grab ;
the first run downloads them into the Grape cache,
.IR ~/.groovy/grapes .
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I NAME
Lower case letters, digits and underscores, starting with a letter.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
The parent directory, default
.B SMI_DB_DIR
or the current directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SMI_DB_DIR
Default of
.BR \-\-dir .
.TP
.B JAVA_OPTS
Further Java options, kept after the ones the command sets.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.PP
The
.B groovy
package, Groovy 6, and the
.B jdk
package, Java 23 or newer.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The database was created and the variables printed.
.TP
.B 1
An invalid name, a directory that already exists, or a failed start.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Create, populate and query:
.RS
.nf
smi-neo4j-create-db -d data graph > graph.env
\&. ./graph.env
smi-neo4j-query < populate.cypher
smi-neo4j-query "MATCH (p:Person) RETURN p.name"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-create-db (1),
.BR smi-neo4j-query (1)
.SH AUTHOR
setmy.info
